Z||000000||Two88GTs||05-02-2001||11:20 PM||||What kind of gas mileage are you guys getting with the 3.33 final gear ratio and the V6 auto?  My results over the last year:<P>26.7 - strictly highway driving the speed limit @55-65mph<P>24 - two lane country roads, 40-45mph most of the time<P>20 - mostly 6-mile commutes during the winter months<P>------------------<BR>88GT 66k<BR>88GT 59k||||reg||1
Z||000001||pHoOl||05-02-2001||11:35 PM||||Well, i have an 88GT auto, but i was never able to determine what gear ratio mine was.  anyway.... i usually get around 22 mpg, and that was mostly country/highway driving.  pretty sad, eh?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||05-02-2001||11:40 PM||||I would say I get about the same.  Maybe a little bit higher on the highway.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Two88GTs||05-02-2001||11:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>Well, i have an 88GT auto, but i was never able to determine what gear ratio mine was.  anyway.... i usually get around 22 mpg, and that was mostly country/highway driving.  pretty sad, eh?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Check the RPO codes underneath the hood near the master cylinder.  GX3=3.33||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||05-03-2001||12:37 AM||||Look for the GX3 code.....also, I believe all '87-'88 V-6's had the 3.33.<P>I have owned several auto. '88 GT's......the best I ever did was 30 MPG (this was travelling a steady 60 MPH).<P>The worst I did was 12 MPG......lots of idling in traffic, etc.  I averaged 23-25 MPG overall with 27-28 the norm on long trips.<P>I'd say your figures are accurate for a Fiero in good working order.||||reg||1
